<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SpotBugs / Find Security Bugs suppressions (#191, ADR-0042).

  Rules for this file:
    * One <Match> per finding, scoped to the narrowest class (and method when
      possible) plus a single bug pattern. Never suppress a pattern globally.
    * Every entry MUST carry a comment explaining why the finding is a false
      positive (not "we will fix it later": fix it or open an issue instead).
    * Entries are reviewed like code. A suppression nobody can justify is a hole.

  How to triage a finding: see docs/16-CICD-PIPELINE.md, section "SpotBugs".
-->
<FindBugsFilter>

  <!--
    SPRING_CSRF_PROTECTION_DISABLED (CWE-352) in the API security chain.

    False positive: the API is stateless. SessionCreationPolicy.STATELESS is set,
    no session cookie is ever issued, and JwtAuthenticationFilter reads credentials
    exclusively from the "Authorization: Bearer" header, which a browser never
    attaches on its own to a cross-site request. CSRF only exists when the browser
    sends ambient credentials (cookies); there are none here. The browser-facing
    surface is the BFF, which keeps CSRF protection ENABLED (BffSecurityConfig).
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="com.menta.auth.infrastructure.security.SecurityConfig"/>
    <Bug pattern="SPRING_CSRF_PROTECTION_DISABLED"/>
  </Match>

</FindBugsFilter>
